#N canvas 20 20 1200 620 12;
#X text 20 20 t_midiout -- a stand-in for [midiout] that prints every byte the patch emits \, with the port it was emitted on. tools/phase6-assert.sh rewrites [midiout] to [t_midiout] in a SCRATCH COPY of the patch \; nothing in Cut It/ is touched and this file is never deployed., f 84;
#X text 20 130 IT CANNOT BE DONE BY SEARCH PATH. mac-stubs/ works because [shell] is an EXTERNAL that is absent on the Mac \, so Pd falls through to an abstraction of that name. midiout is a BUILT-IN CLASS \, and Pd resolves the class table before it looks for a file -- measured both ways \, and a midiout.pd on the path is simply ignored. So the object name has to change \, which means rewriting the box., f 84;
#X text 20 280 creation args: none. inlet 0: a byte \, hot. inlet 1: the port \, cold -- same shape as the real object \, so the port still arrives from [f \$1] at load. outlets: none. It prints rather than sending on a bus \, so a run is a plain text file that tools/phase6-assert.py can read back., f 84;
#X obj 20 420 inlet;
#X obj 300 420 inlet;
#X obj 20 490 pack f f;
#X obj 20 550 print MIDIOUT;
#X connect 3 0 5 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 1;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
